# Intent: the xiaozhi side of the hard mute (maipai_privacy.h, patch 106): while muted or in full quiet AudioService::ReadAudioData reads nothing (so nothing is fed to the wake word), EnableWakeWordDetection(true), EnableVoiceProcessing(true) and SetStopWordArmed(true) refuse, Application::SetListeningMode (the one way into the listening state: tap, wake word, host start, reconnect) refuses and puts the unit back to idle with a 'tap ... why muted' diagnostic, and a wake word that arrives after the mute is dropped. Unmuting needs nothing here: the audio task opens the microphone on its next read and the main task arms the wake word for an idle unit.
# Upstream: xiaozhi-esp32 main/audio/audio_service.cc, main/application.cc (MIT). Applies after 106 and 101 (xiaozhi-esp32 repo).
# Check after a flash: muted: tap the cheek (the rest of the face) and the unit does not listen, the host log shows 'unit tap: decision=ignored why=muted'; say the wake word and nothing happens; unmute by holding the mouth and the wake word works again within a second.
